Sustained study — complete the first course and revisit its models critically (@gc-course-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @general-chemistry, #source "../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94", #source "../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ", #source "../sources/MIT-5-111SC.lingua#r_312Z44VT67CCX60KG27PWM6NZ8", #source "../sources/MIT-5-112.lingua#r_05VDAXGTY0M9E5K9TMJTWTFNAG", #general-chemistry "A-sustained-laboratory-programme.lingua#r_537CX8QFHX4Q7HR6W795QNCY76") { r_3JB6YE4WHPJS0YH8W2FGAY3AM4
**Read:** [Chemistry 2e — Flowers, Theopold, Langley, and Robinson](../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94), the whole book and substantial chapter exercises; [Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower](../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ), the complete first/second-semester text and relevant advanced units; [Principles of Chemical Science — MIT 5.111SC, Fall 2014](../sources/MIT-5-111SC.lingua#r_312Z44VT67CCX60KG27PWM6NZ8), the full course and supplied assessments; [Principles of Chemical Science — MIT 5.112, Fall 2005](../sources/MIT-5-112.lingua#r_05VDAXGTY0M9E5K9TMJTWTFNAG), the full published lecture progression.

Complete the whole OpenStax Chemistry 2e, all 21 chapters, with substantial exercises, and the complete Chem1 first/second-semester text. Use the Portuguese companion in full for its introductory scope. Maintain the connection between equations, molecular/structural accounts, and observations instead of treating problem solving as a catalogue of unrelated formula substitutions.

Work the full MIT 5.111SC lecture/concept-question/problem sequence and independently attempt its exams before consulting solutions. Explain errors and revisit the relevant reading with new problems. The published course provides a concrete undergraduate benchmark; it does not confer enrollment, credit, professional qualification, or graduate-level research competence by itself.

Then undertake the complete MIT 5.112 lecture progression as the stronger second treatment, following missing mathematical preparation where used. Compare its electronic, thermodynamic, coordination, semiconductor, and nuclear explanations with the earlier sources. Its listed campus assessments are not all supplied in OCW; use available material honestly and construct independently justified problems where needed.

**Produce:** a set of substantial original worked studies spanning quantity/conservation, structure/bonding, phases/solutions, energy/direction, kinetics, equilibrium, acid/base/speciation, electrochemistry, descriptive/organic chemistry, and nuclear change. Each should include assumptions, units, an independent check, evidence or a testable prediction, and a criticized approximation. Reconstruct at least one argument in another representation or method.

The laboratory and research studies that follow are additional depth, not replaced by the course examinations. Read the complete relevant source chapters when using a method, and keep edition/right notices and external links clear. Strong foundations should enable exploration across fields while preserving the intellectual work required to defend a detailed chemical explanation.

**Continue:** [Practical programme — obtain, interpret, and defend chemical observations](A-sustained-laboratory-programme.lingua#r_537CX8QFHX4Q7HR6W795QNCY76).

**Return:** [General chemistry](../General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V).
